WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:01.801
One person he does not have

00:00:01.801 --> 00:00:03.003
is his daughter,

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:03.903
Ivanka Trump,

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:04.904
because just moments

00:00:04.904 --> 00:00:06.439
after the former

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:07.240
president said

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:10.076
that he would have run again for 20, 24

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:10.844
his daughter

00:00:10.844 --> 00:00:12.679
Ivanka released a statement

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.948
essentially saying, look, I'm opting out.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.149
She says

00:00:16.182 --> 00:00:17.050
this time around

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.551
I'm choosing to prioritize

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:20.487
my young children and the private life

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.155
we are creating as a family.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.758
I do not plan to be involved in politics

00:00:24.758 --> 00:00:26.226
while I will always love

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:27.627
and support my father.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:28.461
Going forward,

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:31.898
I will do so outside the political arena.

00:00:32.232 --> 00:00:32.665
They are

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:33.600
I mean,

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.200
I remember

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:36.269
when there was all the conversations

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:37.704
of the so-called adults

00:00:37.704 --> 00:00:38.371
in the room

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.572
and the person

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.441
everyone kept on the speed dial.

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:42.442
Aside from Mark Meadows

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:43.376
during January six,

00:00:43.376 --> 00:00:45.478
it seemed to be Contact Ivanka.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.248
You somehow could reel him in in some way

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:49.682
that's not there.

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:51.051
Whether that was true or not fully,

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:51.551
we don't know.

00:00:51.551 --> 00:00:53.053
But that's not going to be there.

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.521
Well, neither will Jared.

00:00:54.521 --> 00:00:56.189
Apparently, between the two of them,

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:57.357
they were probably three fourths

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:59.159
of the Trump administration

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:01.027
and running the decisions there.

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.262
But that's part of what we're seeing

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:04.164
is that even for his own family members,

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:06.733
the shine is wearing off

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:08.168
despite all of the goals

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:10.203
that we saw in that

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:11.271
assembly that that

00:01:11.271 --> 00:01:12.739
that announcement that he had.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:13.740
It's just it's

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.476
the appeal is not the same.

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:18.845
So what can Trump do up

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.113
to be a little bit different

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:21.681
and to set himself apart

00:01:21.681 --> 00:01:22.882
from other Republicans?

00:01:22.882 --> 00:01:23.983
Now, to the point

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:26.152
about his hold on the Republican Party,

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:27.387
it is absolutely there.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.855
But we also saw the Trump

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.123
era drive

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.891
people out of the Republican Party.

00:01:31.891 --> 00:01:33.226
If they didn't sign up as Democrats,

00:01:33.226 --> 00:01:34.294
I signed up as independents.

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:37.297
So outside of a really raucous

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.832
Republican primary,

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:40.834
if Trump winning the nomination

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:43.536
could be a gift to Democrats. Exactly.

00:01:43.536 --> 00:01:45.705
And you're right, as he's driven

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.140
people out of the party,

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:48.641
that's actually strengthened

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.210
his hold on the party

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:51.811
made it much less likely

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.413
that he could ever be elected again.

00:01:53.413 --> 00:01:54.481
I mean, you don't have a Congresswoman,

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.115
Liz Cheney,

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:55.515
your vision

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.150
of political leadership right now

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:59.219
or Congress after this session is over.

00:01:59.452 --> 00:02:00.620
And we're going to have the good night

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.822
in committee on January six as well.

00:02:03.056 --> 00:02:04.357
But I still wonder about

00:02:04.357 --> 00:02:05.859
not only who could take on

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:07.894
from the Republican side, Donald Trump.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:09.295
I know Governor Santos,

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:10.663
he is the shiny object right

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:13.133
now, does not have

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.468
arguably the most formidable opponent

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.070
in his gubernatorial race,

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:17.971
as one would expect

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:20.039
at a presidential level.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:22.308
But you still have to have the support

00:02:22.308 --> 00:02:22.842
in many respects

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:24.010
of the Republican leadership,

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:24.844
the Mitch McConnell,

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.279
who I don't think is there,

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:28.481
the Kevin McCarthy who is undecided as of

00:02:28.515 --> 00:02:30.283
yet, whether he will go in as

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:32.352
Congresswoman

00:02:32.352 --> 00:02:33.453
Stefanik and

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:35.688
say, yes, I'm all in already.

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.290
When you look at the leadership

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:38.992
right now, in power in the Senate

00:02:38.992 --> 00:02:41.161
and soon to be the House,

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:43.463
does he have the support?

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:45.098
Does who have to support Donald Trump?

00:02:45.098 --> 00:02:46.366
That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:47.433
Yeah, I think he does

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:48.434
because for two reasons.

00:02:48.434 --> 00:02:49.736
One, the reason that everybody

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:50.570
already knows is

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.338
there are many members of Congress

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.340
who are afraid to cross him

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.342
because they're afraid of being called

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:59.245
lil senator X or, you know,

00:02:59.913 --> 00:03:01.948
Ron, the sanctimonious or whatever

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:02.815
the nickname is.

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.350
I think you also have a situation

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.452
where Republican members of Congress

00:03:06.586 --> 00:03:07.987
don't want to be primaried

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.422
from their right.

00:03:09.422 --> 00:03:10.557
They fear that much more

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:11.591
than a general election,

00:03:11.591 --> 00:03:12.992
at least up until this point.

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.227
And so you have a situation

00:03:14.227 --> 00:03:15.962
where you want to stay on the

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:17.497
President Trump's good side

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:19.599
so that you don't incur that challenge

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.568
lightly around the situation

00:03:21.568 --> 00:03:23.336
you have as a Republican right now,

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:24.003
a Republican leader

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.905
is they embrace Trump.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:26.573
And this is now

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:28.474
the direct consequence of several years

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:29.742
down the line of him

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:31.311
having taken over the party.

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.478
I want a lightning round here for

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:33.179
what do you think

00:03:33.179 --> 00:03:34.013
the Senate is going to run,

00:03:34.013 --> 00:03:35.315
throw his hat into the ring?

00:03:35.315 --> 00:03:37.584
I don't think Trump will be a post

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:39.285
really? What do you think? Oppose or not?

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:42.055
I can see DeSantis running.

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:42.855
What do you think?

00:03:42.855 --> 00:03:44.524
If he's going to run, he has to go now,

00:03:44.524 --> 00:03:46.226
even though he's only in his mid forties.

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:46.993
Laura

00:03:46.993 --> 00:03:48.795
if you wait too long, it's the Chris

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.496
Christie rule. You miss your window.

